  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bridging integrated water management and food security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to assist the policymakers of the Myanmar Ministry of Agriculture and Irrigation (MMOAI) in improving the connections between agriculture, water management, and infrastructure development. That will help to enable crop diversification and improve farm productivity, food security, and resilience to climate change. The project focuses on strengthening the links between the water and agriculture programmes, specifically those supported by the Netherlands Ministries of Infrastructure and Environment and Economic Affairs. These goals will be accomplished by developing the knowledge base and capacity of MMOAI and other relevant institutions in agriculture water management, irrigation, and drainage within an Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) context. Furthermore, the project will identify potential programmes which may be suitable for future Dutch interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
